  "seoBody": "<p class=\"spec-meta\"><strong>Version 0.1</strong> · Published April 2026 · Last revised 2026-05-26 · Maintained by Quickler Ltd, Scotland · Contact <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">hello@quickler.co</a> · Licensed under <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\" rel=\"license noopener\" target=\"_blank\">CC-BY-4.0</a>.</p><h2>Why a format</h2><p>On site, your phone is the only computer you carry. Much of your work ends up as WhatsApp messages, voice notes and photos. They never become a proper record.</p><p>The Quickler Format is an open way to record a check over messaging, and to lay out the report. It means:</p><ul><li>You do not install or learn an app</li><li>The office gets one clear record</li><li>Insurers and certifying bodies can read the report without special software</li><li>Any vendor can use it, so you are not locked in</li></ul><p>This is a working draft. Comments and pull requests are welcome.</p><h2>What it covers</h2><ol><li><strong>The check definition.</strong> What the user is asked.</li><li><strong>The capture conversation.</strong> How the user answers.</li><li><strong>The report.</strong> The PDF or JSON the office and others receive.</li></ol><p>It does not cover scheduling, pricing or dispatch. That is up to each vendor.</p><h2>1. Check definition</h2><p>A <em>check</em> is a JSON object. It describes one process you repeat. Example:</p><pre><code>{\n  \"id\": \"weekly-van-check-2026-04\",\n  \"name\": \"Weekly van check\",\n  \"owner\": {\n    \"firm\": \"Example Trades Ltd\",\n    \"firm_id\": \"GB-CH-12345678\"\n  },\n  \"fields\": [\n    { \"key\": \"tyres\",        \"label\": \"Tyres OK?\",        \"type\": \"boolean\", \"required\": true },\n    { \"key\": \"lights\",       \"label\": \"Lights working?\",  \"type\": \"boolean\", \"required\": true },\n    { \"key\": \"fluid_levels\", \"label\": \"Fluid levels OK?\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"required\": true },\n    { \"key\": \"odometer\",     \"label\": \"Odometer photo\",   \"type\": \"photo\",   \"required\": true },\n    { \"key\": \"fault_notes\",  \"label\": \"Any fault?\",       \"type\": \"text\",    \"required\": false }\n  ]\n}</code></pre><h3>Field types</h3><ul><li><code>text</code> - free text</li><li><code>boolean</code> - yes or no</li><li><code>number</code> - a whole or decimal number</li><li><code>photo</code> - one or more JPEG or HEIC images</li><li><code>voice</code> - one audio clip, written out automatically</li><li><code>signature</code> - an SVG path or PNG</li></ul><h2>2. Capture conversation</h2><p>The user gets a message on WhatsApp. The system asks one question per field, in order. The user answers by text, photo or voice. The system turns each answer into a typed value.</p><p>A compliant system MUST:</p><ul><li>Let the user skip an optional field with one reply, such as \"skip\" or \"n/a\"</li><li>Let the user fix an earlier answer at any time before the end</li><li>Respect WhatsApp's 24-hour session window, using an approved Meta Business template for longer chats</li></ul><h2>3. Report</h2><p>Each finished check makes a <strong>PDF report</strong> from a fixed template. It holds:</p><ul><li>Firm name, registration number and branding</li><li>User name, mobile number (E.164), date and time</li><li>Each field label, value and any photo or media</li></ul><p>Two extras are reserved for later. Neither is needed in v0.1 and neither is in the reference system yet:</p><ul><li>A SHA-256 hash of the record in the report footer, to show it was not changed.</li><li>A JSON file of the raw record, attached inside the PDF (ISO 32000-1 section 7.11).</li></ul><p>Both are open questions for v0.2.</p><h2>Compliance levels</h2><p>A vendor can claim:</p><ul><li><strong>Quickler-Format Capture</strong> - sections 1 and 2</li><li><strong>Quickler-Format Reporting</strong> - section 3</li><li><strong>Quickler-Format Full</strong> - all three</li></ul><h2>Reference implementation</h2><p>Quickler Ltd keeps a reference implementation. To ask for access, or to talk about using the Quickler-Format mark, email <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">hello@quickler.co</a>.</p><h2>Open questions for v0.2</h2><ul><li>How to record proof that is not a photo, such as CAD files or IFC models</li><li>Sign-off by two people on one record</li><li>More languages than English, such as Welsh, Gaelic, Polish, French and Spanish</li></ul><p class=\"spec-meta\">This document is © 2026 Quickler Ltd, released under <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\" rel=\"license noopener\" target=\"_blank\">CC-BY-4.0</a>. Forks and derivative formats are welcome. Please cite the source.</p><h2>Conformance declarations</h2><p>Vendors are listed here once they file a declaration:</p><ul><li><em>None yet. Be the first.</em></li></ul><h2>Using the spec?</h2><p>Send a conformance declaration to <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">hello@quickler.co</a>.</p>",
